4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.400
Then Archer takes you through the numbers, space, and Myth vs Fact.

5
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.900
Before we dive in, here's the person who started it all.

6
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:25.420
Hi, I'm the founder of Saving Planets. I got tired of hearing it's too late for our planet,

7
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.600
so we went looking for people proving it isn't.

8
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.900
Real solutions, from every corner of the world.

9
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.800
Let's start with the homepage.

10
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.900
It opens on Saturn, with Enceladus shooting plumes of ice toward the page title.

11
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.500
And look at this.

12
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.240
We now feature 231 real solutions across 11 hubs,

13
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:50.300
with new ones like Parker Solar Probe, The SeaCleaners, and WeForest.

14
00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.300
Over to you, Archer.

15
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.300
Thanks, Crimson. Folks, by the numbers:

16
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.200
21 myths busted, 26 amazing facts,

17
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.100
and over 1,000 pages to explore.

18
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.800
Our smarter search matches by meaning, too.

19
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.850
And every page reads in six languages:

20
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.900
English, French, Spanish, Arabic, Italian, and Hebrew.

21
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.220
Students of physics and aerospace, this one's for you.

22
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.120
Learn why the Roman telescope heads to Lagrange point 2,

23
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.620
play in our Orbit Lab, and follow upcoming launches on the live tracker.

24
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.320
Back to you, Crimson.

25
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.220
Thanks, Archer. Now here's my favorite.

26
00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:36.320
Explore every solution on our world map, pick a hub, and watch its solutions light up around the world.

27
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.920
Yeah, that map still gives me the chills.

28
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.920
We take on doom myths with real facts.

29
00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:46.320
Myth: the ozone hole can't be fixed.

30
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.620
Fact: it's healing, say NOAA and NASA.

31
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.020
Myth: if an asteroid were coming, we couldn't do a thing.

32
00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.420
Fact: humanity has already moved one, with NASA's DART spacecraft.

33
00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:06.770
Folks, every solution here helps people and nature together.

34
00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.270
Find one you love, and share it.

35
00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.770
That's how we save a planet.

36
00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.570
Thanks for joining us. I'm Archer,

37
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.170
and I'm Crimson.

38
00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.570
See you at SavingPlanets.com!

